    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d935">

                <pb facs="0727" n="611" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg611"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/13580.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Special Agent Canova to
                        the Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Aguascalientes</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-10-22T19:00:00-06:36">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">October 22, 1914, 7 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>I have been asked if Silliman’s telegram to Fabela of October 7, 5 p.m., is to be
                    considered as a transmission of the Department’s desires or as a stipulation for
                    the evacuation of Vera Cruz. I respectfully recommend that the Department
                    communicate its desires to the Acting Minister for Foreign Affairs through
                    letter to the Brazilian Minister.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Canova</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
